# Repository structure

- `content/` — tracks, topics, source notes, markdown, card items.
- `app/` — GitHub Pages SPA (theory/practice, list/cards, progress, account, theme, notifications).
- Placeholders stay visible for later tabs: community, roadmaps, reviews.
- One topic = one folder: `content/<track>/<topic>/`.
- Commits: English, no emojis, one logical change per commit (content, then app, then deploy). Do not squash an entire track into a single commit.
- GitHub Pages base path: `/learn-tracks/`.
